{% doc %}
  About — the page that says what kind of shop this is.

  Was: `sv-page` rendering the Admin RTE body — an h2 of the brand name
  followed by five h3s and two bulleted lists, in one 760px column. Every
  sentence on it was true and well written, and it read like a document
  rather than a shop that had been thought about.

  ── What the page has to do ───────────────────────────────────────────
  The copy's real subject is not the family, the town or the fabric. It
  is SELECTION. This business does not run a factory; it decides. Four
  sources come in, one shelf goes out, and the whole of the difference
  between them is a person looking at a garment and asking a question.

  So the page is built around that question rather than around the
  brand's history:

    mast     the name, and where it comes from. The gold thread from the
             size guide crosses the page once — the same hand, the same
             story, and the only decorative image here.
    question the one emerald moment (sv-system.css §07). "Would we dress
             our own child in this?" is the page's thesis and everything
             under it is evidence, so it is set as a pull quote on the
             dark panel and nothing else competes with it.
    sources  four, numbered, each under its own hairline. Deliberately
             NOT four equal cards: they are not four equal things, and a
             2x2 of cards would claim they were. Export surplus is
             declared as plainly as our own production runs — an About
             page that hides where half the stock comes from is the
             thing this one is written against.
    ledger   the signature block. What we check, raised on card; what we
             leave behind, recessed into the ground. The rejection list
             is the most specific, most trustworthy copy the business
             has, and on the old page it was a bulleted list two thirds
             of the way down. Here it is half the composition, and the
             elevation does the arguing: kept things rise, left things
             sink.
    hand     who answers, on the letter card.
    talk     the hand-off. Number and address from Admin, never typed.

  ── Rules kept ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Tokens only; every colour, space and face comes from sv-system.css.
  One emerald panel. One decorative image, used twice as one gesture
  (drawn in at the top, its thread trailing out at the foot).

  Business values — the WhatsApp number and the support address — read
  from shop metafields with no `default:` (ARCHITECTURE.md rule 11): a
  default is a hard-coded business value in disguise and goes on
  printing the stale one after Admin is corrected. Each hand-off is
  skipped whole if its metafield is empty rather than rendering a dead
  link.

  Motion per sv-system.css §08 — transform and opacity only, no scroll
  listeners, IntersectionObserver alone. The entrance is armed by
  `sv-motion-gate` as the section's FIRST child so nothing is ever
  painted visible and then pulled to opacity 0; with script off the
  hold is never armed and the page is simply a complete, static
  document.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  # Admin-owned. Never typed here, never defaulted.
  assign wa_raw = shop.metafields.custom.whatsapp_number.value
  assign wa = wa_raw | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-'
  assign mail = shop.metafields.custom.support_email.value

  assign s = section.settings

  # Counted first, so a rail is skipped whole rather than rendering an
  # empty frame around nothing.
  assign n_source = 0
  assign n_check = 0
  assign n_reject = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    case block.type
      when 'source'
        assign n_source = n_source | plus: 1
      when 'check'
        assign n_check = n_check | plus: 1
      when 'reject'
        assign n_reject = n_reject | plus: 1
    endcase
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The number, grouped for reading, derived from the metafield rather
  than typed beside it — a second hand-formatted copy is how the two
  fall out of step. Any shape we do not recognise is printed whole.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign wa_disp = '' -%}
{%- if wa != blank -%}
  {%- if wa.size == 12 -%}
    {%- assign cc = wa | slice: 0, 2 -%}
    {%- assign p1 = wa | slice: 2, 5 -%}
    {%- assign p2 = wa | slice: 7, 5 -%}
    {%- assign wa_disp = '+' | append: cc | append: ' ' | append: p1 | append: ' ' | append: p2 -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign wa_disp = '+' | append: wa -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

<section class="sv-ab" data-sv>

  {%- render 'sv-motion-gate' -%}

  {%- comment -%} ── 00 · The name ──────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
  <header class="sv-ab__mast">
    {%- comment -%}
      The thread is drawn in from the right edge, needle first. Same
      asset as the size guide's opening: one hand, one story. Purely
      decorative, so it carries an empty alt AND aria-hidden, and it
      never loads eagerly — the h1 is the thing worth painting first.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <img
      class="sv-ab__thread sv-ab__thread--in"
      src="{{ 'sv-sg-thread.png' | asset_url }}"
      alt=""
      aria-hidden="true"
      width="900"
      height="900"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async">

    <div class="w sv-ab__mast-in">
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="eyebrow" data-sv-motion>{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h1 class="sv-ab__title" data-sv-motion>
        {%- if s.title_a != blank -%}
          <span class="sv-ab__ln"><span>{{ s.title_a }}</span></span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.title_b != blank -%}
          <span class="sv-ab__ln"><span>{{ s.title_b }}</span></span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.title_a == blank and s.title_b == blank -%}
          <span class="sv-ab__ln"><span>{{ page.title }}</span></span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </h1>

      {%- if s.lead != blank -%}
        <p class="sv-ab__lead" data-sv-motion>{{ s.lead }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Three facts, gold-dotted. Not a list of claims — the three
        things a reader is actually trying to establish in the first
        ten seconds: where you are, who you sell to, how big you are.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.fact_1 != blank or s.fact_2 != blank or s.fact_3 != blank -%}
        <ul class="sv-ab__facts" data-sv-motion>
          {%- if s.fact_1 != blank %}<li>{{ s.fact_1 }}</li>{% endif -%}
          {%- if s.fact_2 != blank %}<li>{{ s.fact_2 }}</li>{% endif -%}
          {%- if s.fact_3 != blank %}<li>{{ s.fact_3 }}</li>{% endif -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%} ── 01 · The question ──────────────────────────────
    The page's single emerald moment. sv-system.css §07 allows one per
    page and this is it — the thesis everything below argues for.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.q_quote != blank -%}
    <div class="sv-ab__q panel-dark">
      <div class="w sv-ab__q-in" data-sv-motion>
        <img
          class="sv-ab__roundel"
          src="{{ 'sv-roundel-ivory.svg' | asset_url }}"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          width="54"
          height="54"
          loading="lazy">

        {%- if s.q_label != blank -%}
          <p class="lab sv-ab__q-lab">{{ s.q_label }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <blockquote class="pull sv-ab__pull">
          <p>{{ s.q_quote }}</p>
        </blockquote>

        {%- if s.q_after != blank -%}
          <p class="sv-ab__q-after">{{ s.q_after }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ── 02 · Where the clothes come from ───────────────
    Four sources, numbered, each under its own hairline and the even
    ones dropped half a step — a woven index rather than a 2x2 of
    equal cards, because they are not four equal things.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if n_source > 0 -%}
    <div class="sv-ab__sources">
      <div class="w">
        <div class="sv-ab__head" data-sv-motion>
          {%- if s.src_eyebrow != blank -%}
            <p class="eyebrow">{{ s.src_eyebrow }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.src_title != blank -%}
            <h2 class="sv-ab__h2">{{ s.src_title }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.src_lead != blank -%}
            <p class="sv-ab__lead sv-ab__lead--sm">{{ s.src_lead }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <ol class="sv-ab__srcs">
          {%- assign i = 0 -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type != 'source' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign i = i | plus: 1 -%}
            <li class="sv-ab__src" data-sv-motion {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <span class="num sv-ab__num" aria-hidden="true">{{ i | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
              {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                <h3 class="sv-ab__h3">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
                <p>{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ol>

        {%- if s.src_note != blank -%}
          <p class="note sv-ab__note" data-sv-motion>{{ s.src_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ── 03 · The ledger ────────────────────────────────
    Kept things rise, left things sink. The elevation is the argument:
    one panel is a raised card on the ground's lighter surface, the
    other is recessed into it. Two lists that would otherwise read as
    equal halves of a table.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if n_check > 0 or n_reject > 0 -%}
    <div class="sv-ab__ledger-wrap">
      <div class="w">
        <div class="sv-ab__head" data-sv-motion>
          {%- if s.led_eyebrow != blank -%}
            <p class="eyebrow">{{ s.led_eyebrow }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.led_title != blank -%}
            <h2 class="sv-ab__h2">{{ s.led_title }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="sv-ab__ledger">
          {%- if n_check > 0 -%}
            <div class="sv-ab__pan sv-ab__pan--keep" data-sv-motion>
              {%- if s.keep_label != blank -%}
                <p class="sv-read-lab sv-ab__pan-lab">{{ s.keep_label }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <ul class="sv-ab__marks">
                {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                  {%- if block.type != 'check' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    {%- comment -%} Inline, not a snippet: two marks, used
                      here and nowhere else on the site. {%- endcomment -%}
                    <svg class="sv-ab__mk sv-ab__mk--yes" viewBox="0 0 22 22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                      <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity=".45"/>
                      <path d="M6.6 11.4 9.6 14.3 15.4 7.9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span>{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if n_reject > 0 -%}
            <div class="sv-ab__pan sv-ab__pan--drop" data-sv-motion>
              {%- if s.drop_label != blank -%}
                <p class="sv-read-lab sv-ab__pan-lab">{{ s.drop_label }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <ul class="sv-ab__marks">
                {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                  {%- if block.type != 'reject' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <svg class="sv-ab__mk sv-ab__mk--no" viewBox="0 0 22 22" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                      <path d="M6.8 6.8 15.2 15.2 M15.2 6.8 6.8 15.2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span>{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ── 04 · Who answers ───────────────────────────────
    The letter card from sv-system.css §07, and the thread leaving the
    frame at the foot — the same gesture that opened the page, closed.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.hand_body != blank -%}
    <div class="sv-ab__hand">
      <img
        class="sv-ab__thread sv-ab__thread--out"
        src="{{ 'sv-sg-thread.png' | asset_url }}"
        alt=""
        aria-hidden="true"
        width="900"
        height="900"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async">

      <div class="w">
        <div class="card card--letter sv-ab__letter" data-sv-motion>
          {%- if s.hand_label != blank -%}
            <p class="lab">{{ s.hand_label }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="sv-ab__letter-body">{{ s.hand_body }}</div>

          {%- comment -%}
            The signature renders only when a name is set — a blank
            field removes the whole block rather than leaving a rule
            over nothing.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if s.sign_name != blank -%}
            <div class="sig sv-ab__sig">
              <strong>{{ s.sign_name }}</strong>
              {%- if s.sign_role != blank -%}
                <span class="sv-fine sv-ab__sig-role">{{ s.sign_role }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ── 05 · The hand-off ──────────────────────────────
    Both routes are plain anchors and both are skipped whole when their
    metafield is empty. Nothing here works only with script.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if wa != blank or mail != blank -%}
    <div class="sv-ab__talk">
      <div class="w sv-ab__talk-in" data-sv-motion>
        {%- if s.talk_title != blank -%}
          <h2 class="sv-ab__h2">{{ s.talk_title }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.talk_body != blank -%}
          <p class="sv-ab__lead sv-ab__lead--sm">{{ s.talk_body }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="sv-ab__routes">
          {%- if wa != blank -%}
            <a
              class="btn sv-ab__cta"
              href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}?text={{ s.wa_prefill | default: '' | url_encode }}"
              rel="noopener"
              target="_blank">
              {{ s.wa_label }}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}

          <p class="sv-ab__plain">
            {%- if mail != blank -%}
              <a href="mailto:{{ mail }}">{{ mail }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if mail != blank and wa_disp != blank %} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {% endif -%}
            {%- if wa_disp != blank -%}
              <a href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">{{ wa_disp }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Motion driver. Reveals once and unobserves — this is a page read
    start to finish, not a canvas to scrub, so nothing replays on the
    way back up. IntersectionObserver only, per the performance rule.

    The hidden state exists only under `.sv-motion-ready`, which the
    gate at the top of the section adds, so a failed script leaves the
    page fully readable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (() => {
      const root = document.currentScript.closest('.sv-ab');
      if (!root) return;
      const targets = root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]');
      if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window) ||
          matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        targets.forEach(el => el.classList.add('sv-vis'));
        return;
      }
      const io = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
        entries.forEach(e => {
          if (!e.isIntersecting) return;
          e.target.classList.add('sv-vis');
          io.unobserve(e.target);
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.12, rootMargin: '0px 0px -6% 0px' });
      targets.forEach(el => io.observe(el));

      /* Fail-safe. A tab loaded in the background defers observer
         callbacks, which would leave whatever is on screen sitting at
         opacity 0. Anything within the viewport shortly after load is
         shown outright; the observer still governs the rest. */
      setTimeout(() => {
        targets.forEach(el => {
          const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
          if (r.top < innerHeight && r.bottom > 0) el.classList.add('sv-vis');
        });
      }, 1200);
    })();
  </script>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Colour, space, face and elevation are tokens only; type comes from
     sv-system.css primitives (.eyebrow, .lab, .num, .note, .card,
     .panel-dark, .pull, .btn, serif headings under [data-sv]).

     Specificity note: the §02 reset is `[data-sv] h1, [data-sv] p {...}`
     at (0,1,1), which outranks a bare class. Anything overriding a
     margin, a colour or a measure on a heading or a paragraph is
     therefore written `[data-sv] .sv-ab__x`, never `.sv-ab__x`. */

  [data-sv].sv-ab {
    /* clip, not hidden: `hidden` would make this a scroll container.
       The thread bleeds past both edges and is trimmed here. */
    overflow: clip;
    padding: 0 0 var(--f);
    background:
      radial-gradient(720px 480px at 88% 2%, rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.13), transparent 70%),
      radial-gradient(760px 560px at 4% 72%, rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.05), transparent 72%),
      var(--cream);
  }

  /* ── the thread ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One asset, two placements, read as one gesture: drawn in at the top
     needle-first, trailing out at the foot. multiply melts the PNG's
     white fringe into the ivory ground — the same treatment the size
     guide gives its tape. */
  .sv-ab__thread {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 0;
    height: auto;
    mix-blend-mode: multiply;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .sv-ab__thread--in {
    top: -6%;
    right: -14%;
    width: min(640px, 58vw);
    opacity: 0.55;
    transform: rotate(14deg);
  }

  .sv-ab__thread--out {
    bottom: -18%;
    left: -16%;
    width: min(520px, 48vw);
    opacity: 0.4;
    transform: rotate(-162deg);
  }

  /* ── 00 · masthead ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__mast {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--f) 0 var(--d);
  }

  .sv-ab__mast-in {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 980px;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__title {
    margin-top: var(--b);
    color: var(--emerald);
    /* One step under the system h1: this sits above a lead and three
       facts, and at 5.4rem it took the whole first screen alone. */
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
  }

  /* line reveal — by LINE only, per §08. The block is excluded from the
     generic fade below so the two entrances never double up. */
  .sv-ab__ln {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .sv-ab__ln > span {
    display: block;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__lead {
    margin-top: var(--b);
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.35vw, 1.24rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.66;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__lead--sm {
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.1vw, 1.1rem);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  /* three facts, gold-dotted.
     Scoped: the §02 reset is `[data-sv] ul { margin: 0 }` at (0,1,1) and
     a bare class loses to it — the rule and its air would collapse onto
     the lead's last line. Every margin on a heading, paragraph or list
     in this file is written the same way for the same reason. */
  [data-sv] .sv-ab__facts {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px var(--a);
    margin-top: var(--c);
    padding-top: var(--b);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.4);
  }

  .sv-ab__facts li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--a);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* Every item carries the dot and the first one's is then removed, so
     that the stacked phone layout below — where each fact is its own
     line — can simply put the first one back rather than inventing a
     second marker. */
  .sv-ab__facts li::before {
    content: '';
    flex: none;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--tan);
  }

  .sv-ab__facts li:first-child::before {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ── 01 · the question ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__q {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    margin-top: var(--d);
    padding: var(--f) 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sv-ab__q-in {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    /* .w is a grid container here; without this its items size to
       max-content and the quote stops wrapping. */
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .sv-ab__roundel {
    width: 54px;
    height: 54px;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__q-lab {
    margin-top: var(--c);
    color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.62);
  }

  .sv-ab__pull {
    margin: var(--a) 0 0;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__pull p {
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__q-after {
    margin-top: var(--c);
    max-width: 48ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.74);
  }

  /* ── section heads, shared ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__sources,
  .sv-ab__ledger-wrap {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: var(--f) 0 0;
  }

  .sv-ab__head {
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--d);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__h2 {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem);
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__h3 {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.7vw, 1.38rem);
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  /* ── 02 · sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__srcs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--d) var(--f);
  }

  /* the weave — evens drop half a step, so four items read as a run
     rather than as a 2x2 table of equal things */
  .sv-ab__src:nth-child(even) {
    margin-top: var(--c);
  }

  .sv-ab__src {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-top: var(--b);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.45);
  }

  .sv-ab__num {
    display: block;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.4vw, 2.8rem);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__src p {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__note {
    margin-top: var(--d);
  }

  /* ── 03 · the ledger ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__ledger {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--b);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .sv-ab__pan {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: var(--c);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
  }

  /* kept things rise */
  .sv-ab__pan--keep {
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
  }

  /* left things sink — recessed, no shadow, and set a step down the
     page so the pair is never read as two equal halves */
  .sv-ab__pan--drop {
    margin-top: var(--b);
    background: var(--cream-2);
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.28);
  }

  .sv-ab__pan-lab {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  .sv-ab__pan--drop .sv-ab__pan-lab {
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__marks {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--a);
    margin-top: var(--c);
  }

  .sv-ab__marks li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 22px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--a);
    align-items: start;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.1vw, 1.08rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-ab__mk {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    /* optical: align the mark to the first line's x-height, not its box */
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .sv-ab__mk--yes {
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  .sv-ab__mk--no {
    color: var(--tan);
  }

  .sv-ab__pan--drop .sv-ab__marks li {
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* ── 04 · who answers ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__hand {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: var(--f) 0 0;
  }

  .sv-ab__letter {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .sv-ab__letter-body {
    margin-top: var(--b);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__letter-body p {
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.1vw, 1.1rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ab__letter-body p + p {
    margin-top: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-ab__sig-role {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 4px;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* ── 05 · the hand-off ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ab__talk {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: var(--f) 0 0;
  }

  /* No measure here: this element is also `.w`, and capping it would
     centre the close on its own axis instead of leaving it on the page
     gutter with every other section head. The measure belongs to the
     copy inside it, which already carries one. */

  .sv-ab__routes {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--b);
    margin-top: var(--c);
  }

  .sv-ab__plain {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-ab__plain a {
    color: var(--emerald);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    text-decoration-color: var(--tan);
  }

  .sv-ab__plain a:hover {
    color: var(--emerald-d);
  }

  /* ── motion ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* The hold exists only once the gate has armed it, so a visitor whose
     script never runs sees a complete page rather than a blank one. */
  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(var(--rise));
    transition:
      opacity 0.85s var(--entrance),
      transform 0.85s var(--entrance);
  }

  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }

  /* The title is held by its line masks instead — it must not also fade
     and rise, or the two entrances double up. */
  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready .sv-ab__title,
  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready .sv-ab__title.sv-vis {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
    transition: none;
  }

  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready .sv-ab__ln > span {
    transform: translateY(108%);
    transition: transform 0.95s var(--e);
  }

  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready .sv-ab__title.sv-vis .sv-ab__ln > span {
    transform: none;
  }

  .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready .sv-ab__title.sv-vis .sv-ab__ln:nth-child(2) > span {
    transition-delay: 0.09s;
  }

  /* ── narrow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    [data-sv].sv-ab {
      padding-bottom: var(--d);
    }

    .sv-ab__mast {
      padding: var(--d) 0 var(--c);
    }

    .sv-ab__q {
      margin-top: var(--c);
      padding: var(--d) 0;
    }

    .sv-ab__sources,
    .sv-ab__ledger-wrap,
    .sv-ab__hand,
    .sv-ab__talk {
      padding-top: var(--d);
    }

    .sv-ab__head {
      margin-bottom: var(--c);
    }

    /* The two title lines are each their own block, so a line that no
       longer fits wraps INSIDE its mask and the reveal reads as three
       ragged lines rather than two. The floor comes down until each
       written line is one drawn line again. */
    [data-sv] .sv-ab__title {
      font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 7.6vw, 2.9rem);
    }

    /* Stacked, one fact per line, each with its dot — a wrapped row of
       dotted facts reads as a bullet list that lost its first bullet. */
    [data-sv] .sv-ab__facts {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .sv-ab__facts li:first-child::before {
      display: block;
    }

    /* One column. The weave and the ledger's step are desktop
       compositions; stacked, they would only read as stray gaps. */
    .sv-ab__srcs,
    .sv-ab__ledger {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--c);
    }

    .sv-ab__src:nth-child(even),
    .sv-ab__pan--drop {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .sv-ab__pan {
      padding: var(--b);
    }

    /* The thread is a desktop composition: at phone width it crosses
       the copy rather than framing it. */
    .sv-ab__thread {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* Reduced motion is handled globally in sv-system.css §10, but the
     line masks are this section's own and have to be released here. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion],
    .sv-ab.sv-motion-ready .sv-ab__ln > span {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV About",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "sv-ab-mount",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Masthead" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our story" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title_a",
      "label": "Title, first line",
      "info": "Both lines blank falls back to the page title.",
      "default": "Named after a child"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_b", "label": "Title, second line", "default": "in our own family." },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Lead",
      "default": "Sahasra Vastra is a small family business in Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala. We bring together everyday and occasion clothing for children from newborn to eight years, gathered from makers and suppliers across India and beyond."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Three facts, gold-dotted under the lead. Leave one blank to drop it."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fact_1", "label": "Fact 1", "default": "Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fact_2", "label": "Fact 2", "default": "Newborn to 8 years" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fact_3", "label": "Fact 3", "default": "Run by one family" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The question" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The page's single emerald panel. It only works while there is exactly one of it — clear the quote to remove the panel rather than adding a second dark moment elsewhere."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "q_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Before any piece reaches our shelf" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "q_quote",
      "label": "The question",
      "default": "Would we dress our own child in this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "q_after",
      "label": "Line under the question",
      "default": "The brand carries the name of a child in our own family. That is why we are careful, and that one question is the whole of it."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Where our clothes come from" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "src_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Where our clothes come from" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "src_title", "label": "Title", "default": "We don't run a factory." },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "src_lead",
      "label": "Lead",
      "default": "We spend our time finding good children's clothing wherever it is made. Our pieces come from four places."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "src_note",
      "label": "Note under the four",
      "default": "Many of our pieces come in small lots, so a design may be available in only a few sizes. Once it is gone, it may not come back."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Hand-picked" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "led_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Hand-picked, one piece at a time" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "led_title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "We look at every piece before it goes on the website."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "keep_label", "label": "Kept column label", "default": "What we check" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "drop_label", "label": "Rejected column label", "default": "What we leave behind" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Who answers" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hand_label", "label": "Label", "default": "A small business, run by hand" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "hand_body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "<p>Our family runs everything here: finding the pieces, checking each one, and packing every parcel. When you message us, you are talking to the people who packed your order.</p><p>We answer within a day.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sign_name",
      "label": "Signature name",
      "info": "Leave blank to remove the signature entirely."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "sign_role", "label": "Signature role" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The hand-off" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The number and the address come from the shop metafields custom.whatsapp_number and custom.support_email. Neither is typed here: a second copy is how the two fall out of step. A route with no metafield is not rendered."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "talk_title", "label": "Title", "default": "Talk to us" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "talk_body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "Questions about sizing, fabric, or an order in transit are all welcome. The people who packed your parcel are the people who answer."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "wa_label", "label": "WhatsApp button label", "default": "Message us on WhatsApp" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "wa_prefill",
      "label": "WhatsApp opening message",
      "default": "Hi Sahasra Vastra, I have a question."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "source",
      "name": "Source",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "name": "What we check",
      "settings": [{ "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Line" }]
    },
    {
      "type": "reject",
      "name": "What we leave behind",
      "settings": [{ "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Line" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
